# 35_wbtb_lucid_gamma.ledc — WBTB Lucid: Gamma-in-Theta split field, ~25 min
# ALTERED STATE: lucid dreaming via a Wake-Back-To-Bed (WBTB) re-induction — a theta dream bed
#   carrying brief gamma "awareness" cues, meant to seed the recognition "I am dreaming" while
#   drifting back to sleep. Scaffolding only. Arc: brief alpha 10 induction -> split-field theta
#   hold with alternating 40 Hz gamma cues -> Soft Off to dark (lucid sessions never wake you).
#
# V2 FEATURES USED (and why):
#   * SPLIT-FIELD per-eye (channel masks) — the LEFT eye flickers theta 6.5 Hz and the RIGHT eye
#     theta 4.5 Hz. Via the optic-chiasm crossover this biases the two hemispheres differently, a
#     Siever split-field technique for holding dream-state awareness (playbook B5). Both rates are
#     safely below the danger band, unlike 30_splitfield_lucid's 16 Hz eye.
#   * LED phase 0 / 180 PHASE-LOCKED ANTIPHASE gamma pair — an amber bank (phase 0) and a cyan
#     bank (phase 180) run 40 Hz in antiphase across a THIRD field region, delivering the "gamma
#     awareness" cue as an invisible (luminance-flat) shimmer that will not jar you awake
#     (playbook B1). This is the phase-locked element.
#   * Audio duty + audio phase — bilateral 40 Hz isochronic gamma CLICKS: two channels at 340 Hz,
#     10% duty (env=0 square gate), one at phase 0 panned left and one at phase 180 panned right,
#     so the clicks ALTERNATE ear-to-ear (a Sana-style bilateral cue) over a gentle theta bed.
#     Audio phase = the relative pulse phase between the two channels (playbook A2 / patent
#     landscape Sana US 11,400,252, used here only as the generic bilateral-alternation idea).
#
# RESEARCH / PATENT CITATION:
#   Split-field per-eye: entrainment_techniques_playbook.md B5 (Siever US 5,709,645, EXPIRED).
#   Invisible antiphase flicker B1. Bilateral alternating stimulus / duty click A2. Lucid WBTB arc:
#   SESSION_DESIGN_GUIDELINES.md §1 (lucid = Soft Off, no wake). 40 Hz offered as an explicit fixed
#   research frequency, framed strictly non-medically (MIT US 10,682,490, patent_landscape_ave.md).
#
# channel_map recipe (menuconfig CONFIG_LED_CHANNEL_MAP): channels are fixed by temperature/eye
#   (ch0=L-cool bit1, ch1=L-warm bit2, ch2=R-cool bit4, ch3=R-warm bit8). LEFT-eye theta = mask 3
#   (ch0+ch1), RIGHT-eye theta = mask 12 (ch2+ch3), both eyes = mask 15. The antiphase gamma pair
#   rides temperature ACROSS both eyes: AMBER (warm) = mask 10 (ch1+ch3), CYAN (cool) = mask 5
#   (ch0+ch2), so the invisible 40 Hz shimmer reaches both eyes. Map LEFT-eye pixels to channels
#   0/1 and RIGHT-eye pixels to channels 2/3, interleaving warm/cool within each eye. Example
#   8-pixel layout: "0,1,2,3,0,1,2,3" (L-cool,L-warm,R-cool,R-warm x2).
#
# SAFETY / CONTRAINDICATIONS:
#   Do NOT use if you have photosensitive epilepsy, a seizure disorder, or a history of photic
#   migraine. Do not use while driving or operating machinery. Stop if you feel dizzy or unwell.
#   EXPERIENTIAL, not medical. ALL flicker rates (6.5, 4.5, 40, 10 Hz) are OUTSIDE the 15-25 Hz
#   photosensitive band; brightness dim (<=20%, gamma pair <=16%); amber+cyan (no saturated-red
#   strobe); light ramps in 15 s / out over the final 5 min; audio fades in 60 s. A lucid session —
#   ends dark and silent, no wake-up. Best done after ~5 h sleep (WBTB), lying down, eyes closed.
#
# Duration: ~25 min.  LED cols: time freq duty bright R G B mask env phase attack
#   Audio: A time freq pan vol mod [ch] [freqR] [wave] [duty] [env] [phase] [attack]
# Ramp convention = animate-on-start (the > prefix sits where a segment BEGINS).

# --- Induction / alpha 10 Hz both eyes (00:00-01:30): fade in ---
0 10 50 >0 60 120 255 15 1 0 3                 # BOTH eyes (mask 15) cool-blue 10 Hz sine; bright fade-in
A 0 200 0 >0 5 1 0 0 30 1                     # ch1 theta dream bed: 5 Hz isochronic (sine gate, 30% duty); vol fade-in
S 3000 default 10 "Rest back and let a calm alpha rhythm settle you toward the dream. You will stay just aware enough to notice."
15000 10 50 20 60 120 255 15 1 0 3             # brightness reaches 20% (>=10 s ramp-in)
A 60000 200 0 80 5 1 0 0 30 1                 # theta bed settled 40

# --- Split field + gamma cues (01:30-20:00): LEFT 6.5 Hz / RIGHT 4.5 Hz + alternating 40 Hz ---
90000 6.5 50 20 60 120 255 3 1 0 3            # LEFT eye (mask 3): theta 6.5 Hz
90000 4.5 50 20 60 120 255 12 1 0 3            # RIGHT eye (mask 12): theta 4.5 Hz
90000 40 50 >0 255 140 0 10 0 0                # AMBER gamma bank (WARM bits, mask 10 = L-warm+R-warm): 40 Hz, phase 0; fade in
90000 40 50 >0 0 220 255 5 0 180             # CYAN gamma bank (COOL bits, mask 5 = L-cool+R-cool): 40 Hz, phase 180 (antiphase, invisible)
A 90000 340 -60 >0 40 2 0 0 10 0 0 3          # ch2 gamma CLICK left: 40 Hz, 10% duty, phase 0, panned left; fade in
A 90000 340 60 >0 40 3 0 0 10 0 180 3         # ch3 gamma CLICK right: 40 Hz, 10% duty, phase 180, panned right (alternates)
105000 40 50 16 255 140 0 10 0 0              # amber gamma reaches 16%
105000 40 50 16 0 220 255 5 0 180            # cyan gamma reaches 16% (matched -> ~invisible shimmer)
A 150000 340 -60 60 40 2 0 0 10 0 0 3         # left click settled 30
A 150000 340 60 60 40 3 0 0 10 0 180 3        # right click settled 30
S 90000 default 10 "One eye quickens, one eye slows. A soft forty-hertz shimmer whispers: notice. If you see a dream, you are dreaming."
S 600000 default 10 "Whenever you realise you are dreaming, stay calm and steady. You are lucid. Look at your hands, and stay."

# --- Soft Off (20:00-25:00): all fields + audio fade to dark (no wake-up) ---
1200000 6.5 50 >20 60 120 255 3 1 0 3         # LEFT fade
1200000 4.5 50 >20 60 120 255 12 1 0 3         # RIGHT fade
1200000 40 50 >16 255 140 0 10 0 0            # amber gamma fade
1200000 40 50 >16 0 220 255 5 0 180          # cyan gamma fade
A 1200000 200 0 >80 5 1 0 0 30 1              # theta bed fade
A 1200000 340 -60 >60 40 2 0 0 10 0 0 3       # left click fade
A 1200000 340 60 >60 40 3 0 0 10 0 180 3      # right click fade
S 1200000 default 10 "Letting every light and tone fade now. Sink fully into sleep, or dream on, aware."
1500000 6.5 50 0 60 120 255 3 1 0 3           # end: left 0
1500000 4.5 50 0 60 120 255 12 1 0 3           # end: right 0
1500000 40 50 0 255 140 0 10 0 0              # end: amber gamma 0
1500000 40 50 0 0 220 255 5 0 180            # end: cyan gamma 0
A 1500000 200 0 0 5 1 0 0 30 1                # end: theta bed 0
A 1500000 340 -60 0 40 2 0 0 10 0 0 3         # end: left click 0
A 1500000 340 60 0 40 3 0 0 10 0 180 3        # end: right click 0
